<html><meta charset="utf-8"><script>ignore this</script><body><p>Synthetic archive written by timecheck, not a catalogue.</p><p>The Example line belongs to Example Brand.</p><p>Reference Alpha belongs to the Example line and uses caliber One.</p><p>Reference Beta belongs to the Example line and uses caliber Two Top.</p><p>Reference Gamma belongs to the Example line, with no documented caliber.</p><p>Beta succeeds Alpha within the Example line.</p><p>Caliber One is made by Example Brand and offers no grades.</p><p>Caliber Two is made by Example Brand and is derived from caliber One.</p><p>Top is a grade of caliber Two and its documented grade name is Top.</p><p>Caliber One has automatic winding, 21 jewels and 40 hours of power reserve.</p><p>Caliber Two Top has automatic winding, 25 jewels and 50 hours of power reserve.</p><p>Caliber One does not have hacking; caliber Two Top has hacking.</p><p>Alpha was produced from 2000 to 2005. Beta was produced from 2006 to present.</p><p>Gamma was produced from 1998 to 1999.</p><p>A competing documented specification gives caliber One 23 jewels.</p><p></p></body></html>